.TH SUBLIME-MUSIC 1 "2026-09-23" "sublime-music @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sublime-music \- native GTK3 Subsonic client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sublime-music
[\fB\-l\fR \fILOGFILE\fR] [\fB\-m\fR \fILOGLEVEL\fR] [\fB\-c\fR \fICONFIG\fR]
.br
.B sublime-music
(\fB\-h\fR | \fB\-\-help\fR)
.br
.B sublime-music
(\fB\-v\fR | \fB\-\-version\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sublime Music is a native GTK3 client for Subsonic-compatible music servers
(Subsonic, Airsonic, Navidrome, Gonic, ...). It plays music locally through mpv
or on Chromecast devices, integrates with MPRIS, caches songs for offline
listening and shows the library by album, artist, folder, playlist or as one
sortable song table.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show the help screen and exit.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Show the version and exit.
.TP
\fB\-l\fR \fILOGFILE\fR, \fB\-\-logfile\fR \fILOGFILE\fR
Write the log to \fILOGFILE\fR instead of standard error.
.TP
\fB\-m\fR \fILOGLEVEL\fR, \fB\-\-loglevel\fR \fILOGLEVEL\fR
The minimum level to log: debug, info, warning (the default), error or critical.
.TP
\fB\-c\fR \fICONFIG\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fICONFIG\fR
Use \fICONFIG\fR as the configuration file instead of
\fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/sublime-music/config.json\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/sublime-music/config.json
The configuration, including the configured servers.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/sublime-music/
The cache: the metadata database, cover art and downloaded songs, per server.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B REQUEST_DELAY
Two numbers separated by a comma, e.g. \fB3,5\fR: adds a random delay of that many
seconds to every network request, to simulate a slow connection.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/sublime-music/sublime-music
